Static fail-closed paths cover shortcut and terminal source families, direct
Root-decision bypass, route substitution, cross-domain binding, foreign ID,
scope/capability widening, recursive-capability removal, mode upgrade and
downgrade, and G2-A/G2-B non-authority. A decision object without the complete
accepted RouteEligibility/source family cannot construct an accepted topology.
RuntimeExecutionTopology owns execution shape but is explicitly not authority.

9. Topology, Queue, Budget, Scope, and Backpressure

Topology identity is derived from the validated source binding, seed, ordered
nodes, ordered edges, assignments, mode profile, and Root-reviewed route. The
root and child cell IDs, topology artifact, source family hash, policy ID, and
profile ID are cross-bound. Foreign, missing, duplicated, reordered, skipped,
or substituted predecessor material fails closed.

Queue state is immutable and predecessor-linked. Current code validates exact
round, state, reason, admission, activation-parent, local-child-result, and
artifact relationships. Latest-settled-prefix validation rejects incomplete,
foreign, duplicate, and reordered material. Scheduler ordering is exact across
the six queue classes.

Budget construction and validation preserve owner, predecessor, local/global
pair, event kind, immutable immediate-parent allocation basis, reserve/release,
revise, and create-only debit laws. The accepted isolated structural matrix is
the exact 1+4+16 tree: 21 unique instantiated cell IDs enter accounting only
after accepted CELL_CREATE; planning, INITIAL_ALLOCATION, and ACTIVATE do not
debit; the attempted 22nd create is bounded.

Scope validation binds capabilities, TTL, forbidden claims, lineage, parent
slot, allocation, and source context. Child authority cannot propagate upward
or sideways. Valid policy/scope/budget denial is distinguished from malformed
structural input.

Backpressure uses bounded max_parallelism, deterministic admission order,
one state per evaluated round, visible deferred PENDING work, dependency wait,
budget-exhaustion BLOCKED, no drop/reorder, and unchanged-state suppression.
Recursion is bounded by max_depth, max_fan_out, max_total_cells, budget limits,
revise limits, and cycle guards. No accepted unbounded scheduler or recursion
path was found.

10. Results, Post V&V, GT, PARENT_RETURN, and Root Boundary

Only actual invoked child results or valid no-child terminal material can
advance a parent slot. Structural corruption creates no accepted slot terminal,
partial failure, result, causal row, or bundle. Actual-only child result and
partial-failure postorder precedes merge, ResultProposal, Post V&V, GT,
PARENT_RETURN, complete-terminal validation, final result, and bundle assembly.

run_fractal_runtime_v02 returns the exact public pair
(bundle_or_none, terminal_report). Accepted COMPLETE_PROFILE requires an actual
FractalRuntimeExecutionBundleV02 plus a PASS validation report. Invalid source
families return no bundle and fail before accepted topology execution.

Post V&V and GT use the additive explicit-time seams for deterministic G2-D
proof. ResultProposal, POST_VV_REPORT, and GT_ADVISORY_REPORT are independently
validated and reconstructed. GT remains advisory and does not prove truth or
create Root authority. PARENT_RETURN is fixed by the accepted Transition
profile. Only the root enters t13-t17 and only Root owns the global outcome.

FractalCellResultV02 is not FinalOutput. A child cannot create Root, permission,
packet, receipt, FinalOutput, DRS write, authority, or effect. Stage D-B and
Stage D-C bundles preserve exact report, artifact, trace, causal, and parent
relationships without changing this boundary.

