14. Authority, Effect, and Zero-Operation Boundary

Static authority findings:
- RuntimeExecutionTopology is a runtime-owned shape, not Root or authority.
- A child cell is bounded local execution material, not Root.
- A child result and ResultProposal are not FinalOutput.
- PARENT_RETURN returns validated advisory/result material toward Root; it does
  not grant the runtime final authority.
- Root remains the sole final/global outcome owner.
- No provider-owned PlanGraph is promoted to topology owner.

Static zero-operation findings:
- G2-D runtime module imports no provider, model, network, connector, external
  DRS, filesystem, random, or subprocess execution surface.
- Runtime code contains no call to its counterfactual validator; profile-aware
  calls occur only in D5 proof construction after accepted bundles.
- Public G2-D and D6 runners import no tests.
- No public runner calls private _d4_run_runtime_v02.
- No exec, eval, compile-based dynamic generation, or dynamic import call exists
  in the nineteen implementation/additive paths.
- D5 report and case counters are structurally required to be zero for provider,
  model, Gemini, network, connector, external DRS, packet, permission, receipt,
  FinalOutput, DRS write, authority, and real-world effect.
- D6 checks preserve and independently mutate/reject those zero-counter laws.
- Topology creation is counted separately and is not an effect.

The Conformance runner has one subprocess.run call at lines 252-265 solely for
local read-only `git rev-parse --short HEAD` implementation-commit metadata. It
does not execute a proof runner, provider, network, connector, or external DRS
surface and has no authority/effect consequence.

Post V&V loads local schemas through bounded maxsize=1 validators and accepts
an explicit checked_at value for deterministic G2-D evidence. GT similarly
parses explicit validated time. Those lower-layer local schema/time operations
are not hidden external execution and do not change the zero-effect boundary.

