Cache audit:
- serialized validation success cache: maximum 4096.
- source-context-family success cache: maximum 16.
- topology-construction success cache: maximum 16.
- topology-parts success cache: maximum 32.
- retained-base-reports success cache: maximum 32.
- all use content-derived, type-tagged recursive keys; cyclic/unsupported
  mutable material bypasses caching; keys are recomputed before storage.
- only successful validation/construction/report tuples are stored. Failures
  and exceptions are not cached.
- deterministic FIFO eviction is applied at each explicit maximum.
- _clear_fractal_runtime_validation_caches_v02 clears every explicit cache and
  both metadata caches.
- the two maxsize=None lru caches hold get_type_hints and dataclass fields only;
  every call site first constrains the key to the finite canonical serialized
  type domain. Their accepted-path cardinality is therefore finite despite the
  implicit decorator bound.
- Post V&V schema validators each use maxsize=1.
- no mutable cache value becomes semantic proof, no object identity is a
  semantic cache key, and no caller selects cached PASS/status/reason.

Fixture/performance audit:
- Five separate D3 module fixtures each build one exact mode micro-environment.
- d3_mode_environments composes those five values and builds no sixth family.
- The full-fractal fixture is constructed once and reused by Profile-D.
- d3_six_class_pairs consumes the composed mapping without rebuilding modes.
- D3 fixtures make zero complete run_fractal_runtime_v02 calls.
- D4 source fixture makes zero runtime calls; the D4 bundle fixture makes one.
- The D5 module fixture invokes the D5 collector once; internally the collector
  performs exactly ten accepted runs and seventeen early-fail public run-pair
  checks, not 72 complete runtimes.
- Living and Conformance test modules each collect one shared D5 report and
  reuse it through module-scoped fixtures.
- No session fixture, nested pytest, or test-spawned subprocess exists.
- D1-D5 mechanisms have focused tests; development does not necessarily require
  either greater-than-20-minute cumulative D6 file.

